        "answer": "# Panchayati Raj\n\nPanchayati Raj refers to the system of **Panchayat institutions** in India, which are the **rural local governments**. These institutions are responsible for deliberating, discussing, and making decisions at the local level.\n\nThe concept emphasizes putting power in the hands of the people through these local self-governing bodies. Article 40 of the Indian Constitution, under the Directive Principles of State Policy, mandates that the State should organize village panchayats and grant them the necessary powers to function as units of self-government.\n\n**📘 Source:** Samacheer Kalvi Class 11 Political Science • Panchayati Raj"
